Subject: [PATCH] iwinfo: query the radio regulatory domain using its WIPHY

NL80211_CMD_GET_REG selects a per-radio domain using NL80211_ATTR_WIPHY.
An interface name supplies only IFINDEX through nl80211_request(), which
can return the global intersection domain instead. Resolve the PHY before
the request so all iwinfo users see the same radio country. Retain the old
request as a fallback if the per-PHY query is unavailable.

--- a/iwinfo_nl80211.c
+++ b/iwinfo_nl80211.c
@@ -3327,5 +3327,12 @@
 static int nl80211_get_country(const char *ifname, char *buf)
 {
+	const char *phy = nl80211_ifname2phy(ifname);
+
+	/* GET_REG needs WIPHY, not IFINDEX, to select a radio domain. */
+	if (phy && !nl80211_request(phy, NL80211_CMD_GET_REG, 0,
+	                          nl80211_get_country_cb, buf))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (nl80211_request(ifname, NL80211_CMD_GET_REG, 0,
 	                    nl80211_get_country_cb, buf))
 		return -1;
